# Line endings are a CI correctness issue here, not a style preference.
#
# Every gate in .github/workflows/ now calls a shell script in scripts/ci/. A
# contributor on Windows with core.autocrlf=false commits those files with CRLF,
# and a Linux runner then fails with "bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M" —
# which reads as a broken gate rather than as a line-ending problem, and costs
# an afternoon to diagnose.
#
# `text=auto` normalises to LF in the repository whatever the local git is
# configured to do; the `*.sh` line additionally pins LF in the working tree, so
# a script is LF-terminated even while being edited on Windows.

* text=auto
*.sh text eol=lf
